    "Fresh JMA institutional Japanese page distinguishes approximate regional200m Tsushima thickness,150m strait seabed,100m thermal index and1985-2010 thermal climatology. Continuous paths are uncommon.0-200m east-northeast60degree is a declared component diagnostic,not a200m bottom,thermal-front classification,current-area index,observed seasonal thickness or full continuous Japan Sea route.",
    "NCC partial58.5-60.75N west-Norway/Trench context excludes Skagerrak/Jutland,fjords,Ingoy/northern continuation and offshore Atlantic branches. Tsushima partial131-134E Japanese Nearshore context excludes Korean/offshore branches,northernJapanSea,Tsugaru/Soya exits and channel seabed as flow boundary. Existing editorial routes provide geographic context,not extracted axes/paired flow edges. Typed identity evidence basis remains explicit.",
    "Frozen complete finite current-specific signed interval requires positive integral and core>10cm/s,without positive surface,relative surface,thermal/salinity qualification. Greatest integral wins with western latitude-cut/southern longitude-cut tie break. Gate/support-edge winners remain unresolved without weaker replacement or post-result retuning. Sensitivities use own seed at same selected column.",
    "Full native0-5000m adjacent finite bracket tracing retains upper/lower contours,statuses,last-supported bounds and paired span without sign/cutoff/missing-gap bridging. Selection endpoints,reported thickness/upper-layer scales,core depths,instrument limits,seabed and missing support are not imposed current bottoms. Same-sign flow can merge currents,so span is not physical thickness or independent named-current validation.",
    "All32targets/both axes preflight jointly under unchanged250000pairs/7MBdecoded,40levels,3-150profiles,20000pairs/patch,5km tolerances. One shared frozen mixed reader preserves max3exactNetCDFIOfailure retries2/5seconds,future first-attempt reserve,no successful replay or per-axis reset. Requested/decoded receipt is not wire traffic or physical precision.",
